1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,750
You can't lift your ring finger?

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,420
Put your palm flat on the desk

3
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:08,570
Fold only your middle finger under
so its knuckle touches the desk

4
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:12,120
Lift the other fingers one at a time
(don't force it)

5
00:00:12,170 --> 00:00:12,970
Fold your middle finger

6
00:00:12,940 --> 00:00:14,890
Lift your thumb

7
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:16,890
Lift your index finger

8
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:18,890
Lift your pinky

9
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:20,890
Now lift your ring finger!

10
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:24,890
Only the ring finger won't budge!

11
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:26,010
What if you straighten your middle finger?

12
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:29,380
The ring finger lifts just fine!

13
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:31,350
The cords that lift your fingers (tendons)
run along the back of your hand

14
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:33,720
The ring finger's cord is tied
to the middle finger's cord by a band

15
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:36,020
When you fold your middle finger,
its cord holds the ring finger's cord too

16
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:38,220
So the ring finger
can't lift by itself

17
00:00:38,270 --> 00:00:41,790
The thumb, index and pinky
have their own cords, so they're free

18
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:44,040
If it hurts, stop right away!

19
00:00:44,090 --> 00:00:46,540
NEXT: Measure your reaction time with just a ruler!
